Behaviour 7 — the drift guard. VERIFIED SOUND.
----------------------------------------------
Broken in both directions and in two extra ways, each from the restored
baseline:
  A baseline                                       exit 0
  B step appended to CI_STEPS only (ci.ts)         exit 1, FAIL names both lists
  C step appended to ci.yml only                   exit 1, FAIL names both lists
  D typecheck/lint swapped in CI_STEPS only        exit 1 (order is guarded, not just membership)
  E ci.ts made syntactically invalid               exit 1, FAIL with `ci.ts: []` —
    the child-process indirection fails CLOSED. A module-load failure is
    reported through check() as a FAIL, never a silent green, never an
    unhandled throw that skips the comparison.
  F restored                                       exit 0
The `node --import tsx -e` child is the right call, not fragile: this
script runs under plain node, the repo's ".js"-specifier-for-".ts"-source
convention needs tsx to resolve, and the only alternative — a second copy
of the list inside the guard — is the exact drift the guard exists to
prevent. Residual nit, fail-closed, not blocking: the workflow side
filters with `line !== "npm ci"` (exact match), so `- run: npm ci
--no-audit` in ci.yml would raise a false red. Wrong direction is the safe
direction, but `startsWith("npm ci")` would cost nothing.

Behaviour 4 — is --ref watertight? YES. VERIFIED BY MUTATION.
-------------------------------------------------------------
gitWorktreeProvider puts the scratch checkout at
<repo>/.bisellium/worktrees/ci-<n> — INSIDE the parent checkout — so node's
upward resolution really does reach the parent's node_modules. The trap is
real and the real `npm ci` is what closes it.

  M1  `(opts.installDeps ?? defaultInstallDeps)(execRepo)` replaced by a no-op
      behaviour 3  PASS  (ref=0 workingTree=1)
      behaviour 4  FAIL  (ref=1 workingTree=1)
      Behaviour 4 catches what behaviour 3 cannot. The install is
      load-bearing and the test proves it.

  M2  `execRepo = worktree.path` replaced by `resolve(repoFlag ?? ".")`
      behaviour 3  FAIL  (ref=1 workingTree=1)
      behaviour 4  FAIL  (ref=1 workingTree=1)
      Both bite; no other behaviour moved.

